(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-harness/src/launch.asl#posixExitCode" :text "procWaitPid (HB5, out of this unit's owns) reports a signal-killed child as -signal, distinguishable from a genuine 0..255 exit; every reap caller here treats its result as a POSIX shell-style exit code, so a signal death is renormalized to the conventional 128+signal (e.g. 143 for SIGTERM) matching launch.py's originally recorded behavior")
